bound: this seat sees REWRITES and TRUNCATIONS of records it previously observed, cross-record INCOHERENCE, and — anchored on --boots and the per-boot nonce ledger (--nonces) — APPENDED .bootlog/.recovery growth the host cannot account for. IN THE NONCE REGIME (the host issues fx.bootnonce= per boot and every window boot is covered) the forged line-PAIR in a silent boot's slack is CLOSED: every ADDED line must wear a nonce the host issued for a boot in this window, per-nonce budgets hold at one in-progress / verdict / shutdown / row, and an unclaimed nonce is REPORTED as a silent boot. What it still CANNOT see: window boots the ledger does not cover (a mixed/manual regime — lines without a window nonce are named and counted, but a forged pair in an UNCOVERED boot's slack still passes the arithmetic); boots started off the counting host, or a miscounted / moved --obs-file reuse (the count and the ledger are only as true as the host's own bookkeeping); a coherent tamper on a store first seen at enrollment (the enrollment gap — first run trusts, loudly). That is the honest bound of auditing, not proofing (§6b), printed on every run so the tool never implies more than it knows.
evidence: the store's own records only — attempts.jsonl (the harness self-report) is never opened.
VERDICT: coherent
